# UI-driver call: select a perceived object instance, activating whichever
# engine(s) claim its perception class and asking each for action
# availability. perception_class mirrors how a perception/UI layer already
# knows an object's class at selection time (see Orchestrator.select_object()).
# More than one engine can claim a class (e.g. "microwave" claimed by
# Articulation, Pick-and-Place, and Microwave Controls), hence the array.

string instance_id
string perception_class
---
bool success
rammp_orchestrator_interfaces/EngineActivation[] activations
string message
